`Assign` from [Ember](https://deprecations.emberjs.com/v4.x/#toc_ember-polyfills-deprecate-assign) is deprecated in Ember 5. Here is a snippet of what it was:

```
function assign(target) {
    (true && !(false) && (0, _debug.deprecate)('Use of `assign` has been deprecated. Please use `Object.assign` or the spread operator instead.', false, {
      id: 'ember-polyfills.deprecate-assign',
      until: '5.0.0',
      url: 'https://deprecations.emberjs.com/v4.x/#toc_ember-polyfills-deprecate-assign',
      for: 'ember-source',
      since: {
        available: '4.0.0',
        enabled: '4.0.0'
      }
    }));

    for (var _len = arguments.length, rest = new Array(_len > 1 ? _len - 1 : 0), _key = 1; _key < _len; _key++) {
      rest[_key - 1] = arguments[_key];
    }

    return Object.assign(target, ...rest);
}
```

**Note:** We decided that because Spread creates a new object whereas Object.assign does not, we are using Object.assign when a new Object was not created and Spread when a new object was explicitly created. See Stack overflow discussion [here](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/32925460/object-spread-vs-object-assign).

```
return assign({}, resp, data); // use spread
return assign(resp, data); // use Object assign
```

